webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7281441Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7293430Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7401523Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7413824Z ^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7414466Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7415236Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7415601Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7415947Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7417551Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7418061Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7418368Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7419049Z    if you are ready to continue.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7419388Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7420034Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7420937Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7421713Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7422486Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7422876Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7423221Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7423580Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7423803Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7424208Z    can use Nix.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7424383Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7424504Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7424692Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7425383Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7426297Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7426941Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7427106Z I will:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7427407Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7427724Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7428392Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7429065Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7429723Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7430213Z  - install Nix in /nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7430714Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7431373Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7431786Z    /root
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7443834Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7444592Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7456729Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7457290Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7457752Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7459101Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7459695Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7478989Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7479537Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7490851Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7491593Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7492276Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7492611Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7492879Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7493283Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7493599Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7494275Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7494641Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7494824Z If you would like to
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7495251Z see the output, try like this:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7495551Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7495807Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T18:03:37.7496429Z   $ sh ./install-nix
